WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.354
Safe serialization in Java starts with
inventory.

2
00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:07.615
Find the places where APIs, queues,
caches, sessions, files, RPC systems,

3
00:00:07.695 --> 00:00:10.150
workers, admin tools, object storage jobs,

4
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.283
and integration paths serialize or
deserialize data.

5
00:00:13.363 --> 00:00:17.412
Identify who creates the data, what format
it uses, what parser reads it,

6
00:00:17.492 --> 00:00:21.606
what object or DTO is created, what
validation runs, what action follows,

7
00:00:21.686 --> 00:00:22.881
and who owns the path.

8
00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:26.412
Avoid native Java object deserialization
of untrusted data.

9
00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:30.739
Where legacy object streams remain, use
narrow filters, class allowlists,

10
00:00:30.819 --> 00:00:34.735
resource limits, authentication,
monitoring, and migration plans.

11
00:00:34.815 --> 00:00:39.195
Prefer constrained data formats and
explicit DTO mapping for external input.

12
00:00:39.275 --> 00:00:42.527
Review JSON, XML, YAML, and binary parser
configuration,

13
00:00:42.607 --> 00:00:46.456
especially polymorphic type handling,
class-name-based binding,

14
00:00:46.536 --> 00:00:49.987
external resource behavior, and broad
object construction.

15
00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:54.912
Validate schemas, versions, fields, types,
sizes, and business rules before acting.

16
00:00:54.992 --> 00:00:58.775
Remember that schema validation does not
replace authentication,

17
00:00:58.855 --> 00:01:03.235
authorization, object ownership, tenant
checks, or business-state checks.

18
00:01:03.315 --> 00:01:07.629
Apply resource limits so oversized or
deeply nested payloads cannot exhaust

19
00:01:07.709 --> 00:01:08.306
services.

20
00:01:08.386 --> 00:01:12.302
Avoid serializing secrets and internal
fields into responses, logs,

21
00:01:12.382 --> 00:01:16.695
messages, caches, dead-letter queues,
support bundles, or exported files.

22
00:01:16.775 --> 00:01:20.757
A practical first-week plan is direct:
search for ObjectInputStream,

23
00:01:20.837 --> 00:01:23.492
inventory JSON, XML, and YAML parser
settings,

24
00:01:23.572 --> 00:01:27.089
disable or constrain polymorphic binding
where unnecessary,

25
00:01:27.169 --> 00:01:31.417
add DTO validation, review raw payload
logging, check message size limits,

26
00:01:31.497 --> 00:01:35.479
test rejected payloads, and document
owners for serialization paths.

27
00:01:35.559 --> 00:01:38.944
Then build serialization review into pull
requests, CI/CD,

28
00:01:39.024 --> 00:01:42.740
dependency review, logging, monitoring,
and incident response.
